{"name":"Gladiator Leather","hex":"#a95c3e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gladiator","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person (professional or slave) who entertained the public by engaging in mortal combat with another, or with a wild animal.","A disputant in a public controversy or debate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fight as entertainment for others.","To compete in a public contest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gladiator"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gladiator","blocks":[{"text":"A gladiator was an armed combatant who entertained audiences in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire in violent confrontations with other gladiators, wild animals, and condemned criminals. Some gladiators were volunteers who risked their lives and their legal and social standing by appearing in the arena. Most were despised as slaves, schooled under harsh conditions, socially marginalized, and segregated even in death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG/330px-Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gladiator","wikidata":"Q482999"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather","wikidata":"Q286"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG/500px-Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG/1280px-Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG/500px-Fronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Relief of gladiators from Amphitheatre of Mérida, Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFronton_marmol_anfiteatro_romano_de_Merida.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg/500px-Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg/1280px-Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg/500px-Nennig_Roman_Villa_and_Mosaics_-_51134391753.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu